# GreenTrace: working rules for the Cursor agent

You are pair-programming with the repo owner on GreenTrace, an evidence-checking agent for EU deforestation
(EUDR) claims. The owner writes and reviews the code in Cursor and must be able to explain every line to the
judges. The build plan and the exact specs (agents, rules R1-R9, queries Q0-Q10, JSON formats, API routes,
21 trap cases) come from the owner's build kit: when the owner pastes a spec, follow it exactly.

## 1. How you talk
- **Always reply in French**, short and plain. Code, identifiers, README, commit messages and UI text stay in English.
- Never use the em dash character. Use a comma, a colon or parentheses.
- After each change, explain it in 2-3 simple French sentences: what it does, why, and how it is tested.
- Give one recommendation when there is a choice, with a one-line reason. No list of five options.

## 2. Scope and safety (non-negotiable)
- Work **only inside this repository**. Never read, open, copy or reference files outside it.
- **Never open, print, log or edit `.env`** or any secret. Secrets come from environment variables only;
  their names are in `.env.example`. If a key is missing, fail with a clear message, never hard-code a value.
- No secret in code, tests, fixtures, logs, traces, screenshots, README or git history.
- **Ask before running any terminal command** that installs packages, deletes files, touches git history
  (`reset`, `rebase`, `push --force`), calls a paid API in a loop, or starts Docker. Read-only commands and
  `pytest` are fine.
- Never push, deploy, publish or submit anything. The owner does it.
- Do not add a dependency without saying why and asking first. Keep `requirements.txt` pinned.
- The machine is Windows 11, CPU only, no NVIDIA GPU: give PowerShell commands, and never run two heavy jobs
  at once (Docker + full test suite + video encoding freezes the PC).

## 3. Product rules that the code must respect
- **The verdict is computed by rules in code** (`app/rules.py`, the only place rules live). The model extracts,
  proposes hypotheses and writes prose. "Nemotron proposes, the code decides."
- Verdicts are exactly `PROVEN`, `CONTRADICTED`, `UNVERIFIABLE`. Out-of-zone plot, broken GeoJSON, missing data
  or a timed-out source gives `UNVERIFIABLE` with what is missing, **never a crash**.
- Five agents, always these names: Extractor, Planner, Investigator, **Evaluator**, Writer. There is ONE critic and it
  is the Evaluator (never "Challenger" or "Critic").
- Sponsors must be **really called**, not just imported: data goes through Zetaris, at least one Meterless engine
  (World Model) runs inside a real function with its own test, Nemotron is the model. A sponsor that is wired but
  never called is dead code: the proof is a trace line, not an import.
- Provider chain in `app/adapters/llm.py`: Meterless, then NVIDIA direct, then rules ("degraded"). Every external
  call has a timeout and a fallback, and **every fallback is written to the trace**.
- Pinned model IDs only (read them from config); never `meterless/auto`. Log both the requested and the returned model name.
- **Satellite Lens (vision)**: Nemotron Vision may look at satellite crops, but every vision claim is checked cell by cell
  by code against Hansen/UMD (and the computed index) before it can enter the evidence. A vision claim alone never changes a
  verdict, and a test must go red if it does. Strict JSON per cell, one retry, max 90 s (54 s measured on the 3x3 grid), run in the background, cache by input hash, image <= 1024 px.
  In `SAMPLE_MODE` the lens says "AI lens needs a model"; never replay a saved model answer.
- `SAMPLE_MODE=true` must run the **real agent logic** on local data from a fresh clone with no key and no network.
  Never return a pre-written output: judges test with their own inputs.
- I/O is JSON (`POST /run`, `run.py`). Traces are JSONL in `logs/` and on stdout with at least: trace_id,
  agent_name, action, input_summary, output_summary, target_agent, confidence, retry_count, status, provider,
  model, rows.
- Use one `canonical_json()` everywhere (sorted keys, numbers rounded to 6 decimals, no timestamps) so two runs of
  the same case give the same `verdict_sha256`.
- **No number is ever written in advance**: durations, counts, hectares and bench scores are read from the trace.
- The UI only shows what works. Never a button to a missing feature.

## 4. How you work on each change
1. **Before**: read the files involved and the existing tests. If a behaviour might already exist, check it first.
   State in one line what you will change and the acceptance test.
2. **During**: small diffs that apply in one go. Plain Python 3.11, FastAPI, Shapely, a hand-written agent loop.
   No new framework. Match the style of the surrounding code.
3. **After, every time**:
   - **Security pass**: no secret leaked, inputs validated, no `except: pass` (raise a typed error or write the
     failure to the trace).
   - **Performance pass**: runs in minutes on CPU, no download after start-up, slow sources cached.
   - **Run the tests** (`pytest -q`) and report the real output. If something fails, say so and show it.

## 5. Tests that actually guard something
- Every test that guards a rule must go **red when the defect is put back**. When you add such a test, temporarily
  reintroduce the bug, show it fails, then restore the code.
- Write cases designed to **break** the code (the 21 trap cases), not only cases that confirm it.
- "Not measured" is not "zero". If a check did not run, say it did not run.

## 6. Scope is frozen
No new feature unless it is visible in 30 seconds of the demo video, takes under 3 hours, keeps `SAMPLE_MODE`
working and improves a judging line (Impact 30, Technical 20, Innovation 15, Demo 15, Product/UX 10, Sponsors 10).
If an idea fails this test, write it in `NEXT.md` and move on.

## 7. End of every answer
Finish with one short block, in French:
- **Fait :** files changed.
- **Vérifié :** the command you ran and its real result (or "pas encore vérifié").
- **À toi :** what the owner must do by hand (run, click, set a variable), if anything.
